# Each playground is its own build served as a standalone static page, not by the SPA.
#
# These paths name the capability, not the library. A library gets renamed — umbra and antumbra
# have already traded places once — and a URL is a promise that should outlive that. So the dialog
# manager's playground lives at /playground/dialog whatever the package behind it is called, the
# bootstrapper's at /playground/boot and the design system's at /playground/design.
#
# A rule here pointing at a directory the deploy does not fill is worse than no rule: the request
# resolves to nothing, falls through to the SPA, and the visitor is handed the home page under a
# URL that promised something else. The list below and the table in deploy.mjs say the same thing
# and are the same length — which `yarn check:capabilities` now holds, after this file was left a
# capability short and the third playground was served the home page under its own URL.
/playground/dialog/ /playground/dialog/index.html 200
/playground/boot/ /playground/boot/index.html 200
/playground/design/ /playground/design/index.html 200

# The bootstrapper's playground was served under the library's name before the capability paths
# existed. Kept so links already in the wild survive. Both forms, because only the trailing-slash
# one would otherwise match and the bare path would fall through to the SPA.
/playground/antumbra /playground/boot/ 301
/playground/antumbra/* /playground/boot/:splat 301

# SPA fallback for everything else
/* /index.html 200
